# What this repository's release needs that another's does not. See propensive/.github, which
# holds the script; a release is cut by `git tag -s X.Y.Z && git push --tags`.
#
# xek releases no jars: a release is the five native client stubs, the `xek` command (as a
# polyglot `xek`, also as `xek.cmd`, and as a native `xek-<platform>` for each platform) and their
# checksums, assembled by etc/ci/client-assemble.sh rather than by Mill's `release.stage`. The
# shared script gates, uploads, verifies every digest, writes the notes and rolls back exactly as
# it does for the jars of the other repositories.

name       xek
title      xek

# Tags are the bare version from 1.0.0. Those up to 0.10 were `xek-<version>`, and those before the
# rename `xeq-<version>`; both are earlier releases too, so the notes of 1.0.0 start from `xek-0.10`.
tag        - xek- xeq-

assemble   ./etc/ci/client-assemble.sh

# The hashes just published go into etc/client/ and res/core/xek/, in a pull request here.
after      ./etc/ci/client-record.sh
